;; A multi-agent TEAM workflow: fan out a worker per sub-task, join the answers.
;; Select with config :run :loop "team" and pass config :run :subtasks
;; ["part A" "part B" …]; run! threads the sub-tasks into the data map and
;; :team/fan-out (cells/team.clj) runs one worker sub-loop per sub-task in
;; parallel, each its own branch on the shared run so they coordinate through
;; the mailbox, then joins their answers into the manager branch. With no
;; sub-tasks it degenerates to a single worker on the whole problem.
;;
;; This is the first, dataflow, slice of the multi-agent work (hc7): workers
;; run to completion and coordinate between-turn via the mailbox. Live per-turn
;; steering (the actor model) is a later step.
{:cells {:start  :loop/assemble
         :team   :team/fan-out
         :finish :loop/finish}

 :edges {:start  :team
         :team   :finish
         :finish :end}}
